# Copy to .env for local development. .env is ignored and never committed.
#
# Rule that is never broken: only the publishable key reaches the browser. The
# secret key and the connection string live on the server (Edge Function
# environment variables) or in GitHub Actions secrets.
#
# This template is intentionally local-only. Production values are supplied by
# the deployment environment and never become repository defaults.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- PWA (web/)
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser. Anything else
# here does NOT reach the client, and it should stay that way.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --------------------------------------------------------- Edge Functions
# These are set with `supabase secrets set`, not here. This section exists only
# to document which ones are needed.
#
# Injected automatically by Supabase, never set by hand:
#
#   SUPABASE_URL
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY     alerts-notify requires it in the Authorization
#                                 header: a valid token is not enough, because
#                                 every employee has one of those.
#   SUPABASE_DB_URL               the direct connection alerts-notify uses.
#                                 `attendance` is not an exposed schema, so
#                                 claim_notifications() cannot be reached over
#                                 PostgREST at all.
#
# Set by hand, once:
#
#   ALERTS_DEFAULT_RECIPIENTS     comma-separated addresses that receive an
#                                 alert when no rule names its own. Today that
#                                 is every alert: attendance.alert_rules is
#                                 empty, and an empty table means "use the
#                                 default threshold", never "disabled".
#                                 Without it the dispatcher refuses to guess and
#                                 reports the failure, rather than borrowing the
#                                 help desk's distribution list and quietly
#                                 mailing attendance alerts to the IT queue.
#                                 The durable fix is a global row in
#                                 attendance.alert_rules; this is the fallback.
#
# The mail account itself is not here: alerts-notify reads it from
# public.config_correo, which the help desk already uses. We are not building a
# second mail system.

# ------------------------------------------------- GitHub Actions secrets
# These do NOT belong in this file. Set them on the repository, under
# Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions:
#
#   SUPABASE_DB_URL      full connection string. From the Supabase dashboard,
#                        Project Settings > Database > Connection string
#                        (Session mode). Used only by the operational backup and
#                        keepalive jobs. CI always uses a disposable local DB.
#
#   BACKUP_PASSPHRASE    long random passphrase used to encrypt the backup.
#                        Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
#                        STORE IT OUTSIDE GITHUB. If it is lost, the encrypted
#                        backups cannot be opened and it makes no difference
#                        that they exist.
